-and hence \(\limsup_i R^\pi(T_i)/T_i\ge1/4\). Remaining work: state whether learners are horizon-aware or anytime, diagonalize if needed, condition on the fixed prior prefix for randomized learners, and write the cross-block pending-reward accounting carefully.
+and hence \(\limsup_i R^\pi(T_i)/T_i\ge1/4\). Iteration 3 reduced the main accounting obstruction: lower-bound the comparator using only the current block, and upper-bound all learner rewards attributable to the previous prefix by \(M_i\). Remaining work: state process-unaware quantifiers, couple randomized learners across the two continuations after the fixed prefix, handle horizon-indexed learner families separately, and write the induction formally. Each sequence in the block class has \(\beta(h)=1\) and \(\gamma(h)\ge1/4\) for all \(h\), but the theorem would be class-uniform/minimax only.
+
+**CL-018: Concatenated same-path horizon-oblivious lower bound.**  
